{"id": "section-body-06419", "title": "Parkinson’s Disease and other movement disorders", "chapterId": "chapter-eight", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "NERVOUS SYSTEM DISEASE CONDITIONS", "Management of Epilepsy", "Parkinson’s Disease and other movement disorders"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-06419", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Parkinson’s Disease and other movement disorders", "runs": [{"text": "Parkinson’s"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Disease"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "other"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "movement"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "disorders"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1659"}}, {"id": "body-06420", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Parkinson’s disease (PD) is a common chronic, progressive, neurodegenerative disorder in geriatric population, characterized by the loss of dopaminergic neurons from the substantia nigra that subsequently results in the loss of control of voluntary movement over time", "runs": [{"text": "Parkinson’s"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "disease"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PD)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "common"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "chronic,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "progressive,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "neurodegenerative"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "disorder"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "geriatric"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "population,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "characterized by the loss of dopaminergic neurons from the substantia nigra that subsequently results in the loss of control of voluntary movement over time"}]}, {"id": "body-06422", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-06423", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Motor symptoms: Resting Tremor